WEBVTT

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.390
Tsubaki!

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.110
Go, Tsubaki!

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.240
He's fast!

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.250
Wind? Or is it a torpedo?

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:23.870
Hiraga!

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:27.170
This will work!

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:28.780
Okay!

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.730
Alright!

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.120
That's a good spot!

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.990
Nice one, Tsubaki!

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.680
Nice! Be proud of that, Tsubaki!

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.240
Your speed and stamina have earned us that free kick!

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.010
I'm taking out Hiraga and Hauer.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:51.270
We are going to hold on to our one-goal lead for the remaining 10 minutes.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.530
Don't get me wrong,

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.280
we're not changing our team's philosophy yet.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.130
It only means that we've come to a stage...

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.820
where it's possible for us to experience games like this.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.540
After all, the season is far from over.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:10.880
Katsuragi and Minami.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.500
Go get Katsuragi and Minami!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.430
Got it!

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.330
I'm sure he wasn't lying,

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.300
but considering it's Dulfer, it's quite unexpected.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:26.860
He's scrapping his philosophy in the hope of securing victory today.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:33.480
And the one who pushed him to such an extent is...

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.860
Focus! Make sure to leave no gaps!

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.500
He's mysterious indeed, Takeshi Tatsumi.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.480
Saka, to the right! Another step to the right! That's good!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.690
Akasaki will shoot! His shots are really accurate today!

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.130
Accurate? The one who's really accurate is...

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.670
Man, this is tough.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.350
When I first heard about this plan, I thought it sounded fun.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.480
My pass completion rate goes down...

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.960
...when I intentionally put them in weird places.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.940
As I thought, Gino wasn't having an off day.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.160
No! It's Gino, Ima!

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.990
He's the one in top form today!

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.200
He'll definitely take the shot!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.000
But the one who put down the ball is...

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.750
That's what they want us to think!

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.500
I can't believe he's falling for it.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:45.570
Either way, they'll probably aim for the goal directly.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.010
I can react in time if I predict their moves.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.580
Are you subbing Hiraga off?

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:56.520
We definitely have to score from this then.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.020
It's not Akasaki!

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.760
It's Gino!

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.780
I've decided, ever since I saw your face in the second half,

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.910
you're the only one for this situation.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.430
YEAH!

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:33.920
We caught up!

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.930
We are level now!

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.170
Good job, Sugie!

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.690
Nice one, Sugie!

00:05:53.550 --> 00:06:02.530
Good job.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:03.960
Job well done.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:07.330
Good job, Sugie, Akasaki.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.130
Wow, I'm surprised.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:22.130
They actually caught up... I thought it'd be impossible.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.480
Not bad, ETU.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.330
What kind of attitude is that?

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.490
Aren't you ETU's reporter?

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.890
But these series of substitutions...

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:37.490
At first glance, it looks like both managers are revealing their trumps cards,

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.000
but the difference in momentum is evident.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.100
Ironic indeed, eh?

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:48.480
Now, ETU is going all out to turn the game,

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:51.520
while Osaka, who was dominating the match in the first half,

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.300
is now enforcing their defense to preserve a draw.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.750
The first card: By sending in the defensive Ootomo,

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.520
it acted as a signal to the Osaka's players to hang on to their lead.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.310
Now that they've been cornered,

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:09.150
going on the offensive again is not going to work out.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.700
As I thought, the decisive moment here...

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.160
...was Dulfer's hesitation to take out Hiraga.

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.410
If that was what he intended to do,

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:26.850
then his plan wasn't aiming at taking down Kubota or Hiraga,

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:32.930
but at Dulfer's strategy itself.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.320
Oh, I might be able to write an article with this.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:39.820
Though it might all be retrospective.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.940
But, you know...

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.820
I really doubt they can manage an upset.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.440
Cut it out already!

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.810
I can understand the decision to bring on Hotta and Miyano,

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.700
but why don't they swap forwards instead?

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.450
That would have threatened their opponent more.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.960
Damn, I guess I won't play today.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.740
I thought that I'd get to play since Natsuki was not playing well,

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.080
but I guess he got his form back.

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:20.300
What the hell? He's out of breath.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.100
Geez...

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.600
Do your job, since you're on the field!

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.970
Tan and Hotta, also Miyano...

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:39.920
I knew it! We've already used up our substitutions.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.370
That means...

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.250
I made it through...

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.120
I wasn't subbed out!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:51.130
Alright! I'm playing the whole match, an important one at that!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.490
Wait, what am I thinking about?! I'm such an idiot!

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:57.390
This isn't the time to be happy about something like this!

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:00.810
Sera! We're going to move Tsubaki up further up,

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.890
so you go play right behind Natsuki!

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:04.730
Got it!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.590
There's not much time left.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.900
Who knows how many chances we'll get.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:16.150
I've got to do it! This is when forwards stand up to be counted!

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:23.740
Shit, don't get tired now! It's stupid!

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:37.980
Why does the manager use someone like me?

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:43.600
Hey!

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:47.210
What the hell, Osaka?!

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.190
Stop wasting time just to get a draw!

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.180
Indeed. That's cheap!

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:53.960
It's not cheating, but you suck!

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.180
But, you know?

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:59.820
ETU doesn't have a history of causing upsets, right?

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:02.550
Hm, I guess so...

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:04.240
It often ends in a draw.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:09.750
And on top of that, their defense has Terauchi and Komura who are both national players.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.020
Ugh, that's true.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:14.720
But we came back from two goals down!

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:17.270
That's true,

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.590
but if they employ an ultra-defensive strategy...

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:29.650
Argh, we're running out of time.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.360
One more! One more! Can we do it, Manager?

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:39.810
My plan was to come back from just a one-goal deficit to win at 2-1,

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.620
so I really don't know about the 3rd goal.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:47.150
D-Don't you have anything up your sleeve?

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.730
We've built up so much momentum!

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:52.880
What's with you? I'm not god, you know!

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:57.630
But I am counting on him.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:10:59.630
Him?

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:08.920
His tenacity is the last strength that ETU lacks.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:12.230
Huh? Who are you talking about?

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:19.190
They're coming from the back! Watch out for their counter!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.030
No! A counter!

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.460
Alright! I've been waiting for this!

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:34.570
Did you really think I'd let you do as you want?

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:36.440
Damn!

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:37.230
Hey!

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.390
Pass it back for now!

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:46.640
Alright!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.090
Yes!

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:49.270
Nice, Murakoshi!

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.650
This is funny.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:00.820
Huh? What is, Kudo?

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:02.650
Well, it's just...

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:08.390
It's still a draw, yet there's a sense of urgency in Osaka's play.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:15.920
On the other hand, the ETU players are all riled up.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:22.220
Or rather, they might be really enjoying this game.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:34.690
We don't have time! Send it to the center!

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:42.780
Nice, Gino!

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.650
Natsuki, sink it in!

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.490
He just can't win in the air.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:52.000
As I thought, I shouldn't have passed it to Natsu.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.380
Yeah, Sera!

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:06.420
Damn it!

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.650
We're pushing so hard!

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.970
Osaka's defense is really tight!

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:14.540
Geez, that was so close!

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:18.600
I guess a situation like that is hard for someone small like Sera.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.100
That's not true.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.860
Not true at all.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:29.060
We've got 4 minutes of injury time! We can do this!

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.620
Attack, guys!

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:33.350
Who the hell is ETU anyway?!

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.620
Show them that we're in a different league!

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.380
Damn it! Focus!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.130
I have to get to the ball first before some big guy runs into me.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.380
I'm not physically strong...

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:52.510
I don't have much technique either.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:57.140
I'm also short and stupid.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:02.890
I basically lack in every aspect that is required of a professional.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:09.530
I don't have any talent!

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:17.850
It's true that Sera is not gifted physically.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:18.760
Huh?

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:20.040
But, you know,

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:26.030
players like Sera know what they can't do.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:29.230
That means...

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:32.300
...they know of their limitations.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:35.180
That's why they won't hesitate on the field.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:39.680
Since they don't have much options, they react much faster.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:41.520
Just like the one before.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:47.800
He was able to compete for the loose ball because he reacted quickly to it.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.630
I see...

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:54.580
Players like him are probably born with an inferiority complex.

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:59.110
They keep eliminating things they can't do...

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:01.830
and only work on the things they can do.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.840
There is nothing that won't shine if you polish it enough.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.220
That's why I'm hoping...

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:16.600
that someone like him will surpass those with talent.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:22.100
The effort of a player like him will make the team stronger.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:27.800
Osaka's defense is focused.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:31.990
ETU will have to think of something to break it down.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.490
Something... unexpected.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.820
Nice cut, Koshi!

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:40.870
Go ahead!

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.620
Murakoshi is going to the front!

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.380
Get on your marks!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.130
Watch out in the center! Block his course!

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:51.590
Come! Focus on me!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:57.930
Good pass!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:00.560
Okay!

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.740
Shoot, Tsubaki!

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:08.690
So close!

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:16.950
I don't have any talent.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:21.770
Go!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:24.000
It's a miracle that I can play on the pro level.

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:28.750
But...

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:32.480
The manager is letting someone like me play.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:47.520
Maybe then...

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:51.790
Maybe believing in a player like myself is fine after all!

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:56.490
A player... just like me!

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:42.450
SERA!

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.500
He did it!

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:51.000
You idiot! You did the impossible!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.000
Amazing! You were amazing, Sera!

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:54.170
It's an upset!

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:54.870
Yeah!

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:56.420
I did it! I did it!

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.140
I did it right at the death!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:07.890
I'm... I'm amazing! I did it, everyone!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.400
Well played, ETU!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:21.660
It's... It's over.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:27.540
That means we've... won!

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:32.920
Alright! We won! It's a huge upset!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.980
Impressive!

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:44.180
They've obtained a big scalp in the form of the once-invincible Osaka.

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:49.440
Unbelievable... Is this really ETU?

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:52.540
ETU have changed.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:53.450
Huh?

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.940
It's time you accepted that, Yamai.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:19:01.520
ETU will surely be the center of the storm.

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:05.590
And I have my eyes on him,

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:11.000
the one who'll become their core and pull the team together.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:23.110
Sera! Good job!

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:24.820
Nice goal, Sera!

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:29.030
Thank you, fans! I love you all!

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:30.540
Hey, Sera!

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:34.480
Didn't you say that you'd do a backflip if you scored?

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:39.390
He's right. Maybe this goal is worth doing it.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.990
C-Can I do it now?

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.340
Now?

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:46.780
Don't expect much though since it's not completed yet.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:49.120
Not completed?

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.890
Okay, I'll do it!

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:52.750
Hey, man-of-the-match.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:55.500
Shit, it hurts!

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:58.110
S-Sakai.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:03.170
You know, you were kicked hard when you scored that goal.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:07.470
If your silly performance results in further injuries, what will happen?

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:12.100
You still don't know what it means to a pro, do you?

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.300
I got scolded already...

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.690
But, you know...

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.980
Diving in, knowing that you'll be kicked...

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:21.920
Only idiots could pull that off.

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:30.270
You've realized what it truly means to be a forward.

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:32.410
I'll give you credit for that.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.670
You know, the ball...

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:42.520
...will always roll towards the person who never gives up.

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:47.760
Sakai!

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:48.910
What?

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.630
The ball really came!

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.550
Thanks!

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:58.460
What was that for?! And I just praised you too...

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:01.660
I'm sorry! You got it all wrong, it's a misunderstanding!

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.490
What the hell are you talking about?!

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:39.020
Sonoda...

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:40.560
Yes, Manager?

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:47.300
I am extremely frustrated right now... especially with myself.

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:52.330
This would not have happened if I was more decisive.

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:54.830
But, you know...

00:21:55.350 --> 00:22:01.090
At the same time, I feel really satisfied.

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:08.090
I understand. It was a good game fought at the very highest level.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:17.020
The next time we meet, it'll be at our home in Osaka,

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:19.100
Takeshi Tatsumi.

00:22:20.320 --> 00:22:24.900
How was it? Was Dulfer spewing a bunch of excuses?

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:27.990
No, he just glared fiercely at me.

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:30.310
Seems like our next match will be a bother again.

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:32.620
Man, those managers who just refuse to lose...

00:22:34.170 --> 00:22:36.490
But it has to be like that,

00:22:36.490 --> 00:22:38.370
or it wouldn't be fun defeating them.

00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:46.560
I'm looking forward to the next match.

00:24:15.360 --> 00:24:19.670
Akasaki has been called up to the team that'll represent Japan in the Olympics.

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:22.320
I've never heard about this!

00:24:22.510 --> 00:24:25.700
Hey! We're going to make curry for 100 people,

00:24:25.700 --> 00:24:28.070
so those who are free, help out!
